r/value "p=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28b5cb1b-dea4-5ec8-a35c-ed97039896c5" :answer/id #uuid "28b5cb1b-dea4-5ec8-a35c-ed97039896c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43c782ab-6da0-58e5-a099-7617877f63a1" :answer/id #uuid "43c782ab-6da0-58e5-a099-7617877f63a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064270 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c86d9a3a-c5bd-5503-9489-53c383f2b865" "question-14e3fc47-0564-56b4-b83c-8a7fa94d57dd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c86d9a3a-c5bd-5503-9489-53c383f2b865" :question/id #uuid "c86d9a3a-c5bd-5503-9489-53c383f2b865" :question/math-academy-id "q-101731" :question/problem "Find an interval where the average rate of change of $f(x)$ equals $0$ given the following table of values of $f(x):$\n\n| $x$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,4\\,$ | $\\,6\\,$ | $\\,8\\,$ | $\\,10\\,$ | $\\,12\\,$ | $\\,14\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\,4\\,$ | $\\,-3\\,$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,6\\,$ | $\\,-4\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,6\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=0$ if and only if $Δf=0.$ So\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & Δf=0 \\\\  & f(b)-f(a)=0 \\\\  & f(b)=f(a).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means we have to find an interval  $[a,b]$ such that $f(a)=f(b).$\n\nSince $f(8)=f(14)=6,$ we conclude that $\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=0$ on the interval $[8,14].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b8f59edb-d323-5390-82ef-191a6129749f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b8f59edb-d323-5390-82ef-191a6129749f" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8f59edb-d323-5390-82ef-191a6129749f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d783a813-ce2c-5f34-b477-df1d5c70b89e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6b167927-7e47-5183-89f2-11a8741c549b" "answer-3d567c88-9f2a-5e56-9977-53ab3e3387aa" "answer-43721b7e-538b-5957-8de2-c684dfdc9889" "answer-d783a813-ce2c-5f34-b477-df1d5c70b89e" "answer-0e6ccc69-9f1d-5d1e-a310-05f931d5a099"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b167927-7e47-5183-89f2-11a8741c549b" :answer/id #uuid "6b167927-7e47-5183-89f2-11a8741c549b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[2,10]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d567c88-9f2a-5e56-9977-53ab3e3387aa" :answer/id #uuid "3d567c88-9f2a-5e56-9977-53ab3e3387aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[4,12]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43721b7e-538b-5957-8de2-c684dfdc9889" :answer/id #uuid "43721b7e-538b-5957-8de2-c684dfdc9889" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[6,8]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d783a813-ce2c-5f34-b477-df1d5c70b89e" :answer/id #uuid "d783a813-ce2c-5f34-b477-df1d5c70b89e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[8,14]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e6ccc69-9f1d-5d1e-a310-05f931d5a099" :answer/id #uuid "0e6ccc69-9f1d-5d1e-a310-05f931d5a099" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There is no such interval" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-14e3fc47-0564-56b4-b83c-8a7fa94d57dd" :question/id #uuid "14e3fc47-0564-56b4-b83c-8a7fa94d57dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-101733" :question/problem "Find the interval where the average rate of change of $f(x)$ equals $0$ given the following table of values of $f(x):$\n\n| $x$ | $\\,-3\\,$ | $\\,-2\\,$ | $\\,-1\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,3\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,-1\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,-1\\,$ | $\\,3\\,$ | $\\,4\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=0$ if and only if $Δf=0.$ So\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & Δf=0 \\\\  & f(b)-f(a)=0 \\\\  & f(b)=f(a).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means we have to find an interval  $[a,b]$ such that $f(a)=f(b).$\n\nSince $f(-2)=f(0)=-1,$ we conclude that $\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=0$ on the interval $[-2,0].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-036ab766-0259-55f6-8113-94c9afa97abc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-036ab766-0259-55f6-8113-94c9afa97abc" :answer-field/id #uuid "036ab766-0259-55f6-8113-94c9afa97abc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fb5ad1f9-b7b2-5c15-a53e-1f3a9f44b473" :answer-field/choices ["answer-17d6b3cd-6f8f-590e-bb5d-743d31b08523" "answer-fb5ad1f9-b7b2-5c15-a53e-1f3a9f44b473" "answer-0e225497-e1ac-5eb6-9cb3-5c89fd6eef24" "answer-8cc10ac0-f906-557a-b5b7-edf62f818cc2" "answer-4ab88dbb-34ea-5c23-bf26-1597dd63a935"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17d6b3cd-6f8f-590e-bb5d-743d31b08523" :answer/id #uuid "17d6b3cd-6f8f-590e-bb5d-743d31b08523" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-1,1]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb5ad1f9-b7b2-5c15-a53e-1f3a9f44b473" :answer/id #uuid "fb5ad1f9-b7b2-5c15-a53e-1f3a9f44b473" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-2,0]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e225497-e1ac-5eb6-9cb3-5c89fd6eef24" :answer/id #uuid "0e225497-e1ac-5eb6-9cb3-5c89fd6eef24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[0,3]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8cc10ac0-f906-557a-b5b7-edf62f818cc2" :answer/id #uuid "8cc10ac0-f906-557a-b5b7-edf62f818cc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[1,2]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ab88dbb-34ea-5c23-bf26-1597dd63a935" :answer/id #uuid "4ab88dbb-34ea-5c23-bf26-1597dd63a935" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There is no such interval" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-9952931b-e374-52ae-a9be-1856f7ea1fba" :activity/id #uuid "9952931b-e374-52ae-a9be-1856f7ea1fba" :activity/title "The Average Rate of Change of a Function" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050572 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-52db5357-a58c-5010-8c13-0de7f7895700" "step-8e9f58a5-83f2-5f0f-a9bc-6158da91961d" "step-da35fb1b-8325-5c95-8113-934e8ad42985"] :activity/first-step "step-52db5357-a58c-5010-8c13-0de7f7895700" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-52db5357-a58c-5010-8c13-0de7f7895700" :step/id #uuid "52db5357-a58c-5010-8c13-0de7f7895700" :step/content 17592186233607 :step/next "step-8e9f58a5-83f2-5f0f-a9bc-6158da91961d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8e9f58a5-83f2-5f0f-a9bc-6158da91961d" :step/id #uuid "8e9f58a5-83f2-5f0f-a9bc-6158da91961d" :step/content "question-c86d9a3a-c5bd-5503-9489-53c383f2b865" :step/next "step-da35fb1b-8325-5c95-8113-934e8ad42985" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-da35fb1b-8325-5c95-8113-934e8ad42985" :step/id #uuid "da35fb1b-8325-5c95-8113-934e8ad42985" :step/content "question-14e3fc47-0564-56b4-b83c-8a7fa94d57dd" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166931 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d4b0fddb-f441-5332-9904-2f366a824fe8" "question-229cdf1d-b683-5de3-b351-27b1d6a26233"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d4b0fddb-f441-5332-9904-2f366a824fe8" :question/id #uuid "d4b0fddb-f441-5332-9904-2f366a824fe8" :question/math-academy-id "q-331950" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{4(s-2)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2={X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-4=-2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-1){X}_{1}(s)-3{X}_{2}(s)=2 \\\\ 2{X}_{1}(s)+(s-1){X}_{2}(s)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{4-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-1)[\\frac{4-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)}{2}]-3{X}_{2}(s) & =2 \\\\ 4(s-1)-(s-1)^{2}{X}_{2}(s)-6{X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ 4(s-1)-[(s-1)^{2}+6]{X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ 4(s-1)-({s}^{2}-2s+7){X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ -({s}^{2}-2s+7){X}_{2}(s) & =4-4(s-1) \\\\ -({s}^{2}-2s+7){X}_{2}(s) & =-4s+8 \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{4(s-2)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{4-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-(s-1)\\cdot \\frac{4(s-2)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4({s}^{2}-2s+7)-(s-1)\\cdot 4(s-2)}{2({s}^{2}-2s+7)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}-8s+28-4(s-1)(s-2)}{2({s}^{2}-2s+7)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4s+20}{2({s}^{2}-2s+7)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(s+5)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2(s+5)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{4(s-2)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f1988ed4-093d-51e3-9639-cb7ca3f1716c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f1988ed4-093d-51e3-9639-cb7ca3f1716c" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1988ed4-093d-51e3-9639-cb7ca3f1716c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-03a9d88d-8478-534d-b20a-f7e25d74ee09" :answer-field/choices ["answer-03a9d88d-8478-534d-b20a-f7e25d74ee09"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03a9d88d-8478-534d-b20a-f7e25d74ee09" :answer/id #uuid "03a9d88d-8478-534d-b20a-f7e25d74ee09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2s+10}{s^2-2s+7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-229cdf1d-b683-5de3-b351-27b1d6a26233" :question/id #uuid "229cdf1d-b683-5de3-b351-27b1d6a26233" :question/math-academy-id "q-332026" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2(2s-3)}{s(s-5)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-4=2{X}_{1}(s)-3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+2=-2{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-2){X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)=4 \\\\ 2{X}_{1}(s)+(s-3){X}_{2}(s)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{-2-(s-3){X}_{2}(s)}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-2)[\\frac{-2-(s-3){X}_{2}(s)}{2}]+3{X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ (s-2)[-2-(s-3){X}_{2}(s)]+6{X}_{2}(s) & =8 \\\\ -2(s-2)-[(s-2)(s-3)-6]{X}_{2}(s) & =8 \\\\ -({s}^{2}-5s){X}_{2}(s) & =8+2(s-2) \\\\ -s(s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =2s+4 \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2(s+2)}{s(s-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-2-(s-3){X}_{2}(s)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-(s-3)\\cdot \\frac{-2(s+2)}{s(s-5)}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2s(s+5)+2(s-3)(s+2)}{2s(s-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(2s-3)}{s(s-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2(2s-3)}{s(s-5)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-2(s+2)}{s(s-5)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-337fbbd0-2104-528d-b75a-5b62951f2ab9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-337fbbd0-2104-528d-b75a-5b62951f2ab9" :answer-field/id #uuid "337fbbd0-2104-528d-b75a-5b62951f2ab9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d461234f-027a-557e-9d34-651597fcb58b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d461234f-027a-557e-9d34-651597fcb58b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d461234f-027a-557e-9d34-651597fcb58b" :answer/id #uuid "d461234f-027a-557e-9d34-651597fcb58b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{-2(s+2)}{s(s-5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166932 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d0737b10-0304-5e2e-a18d-ef1cf02a07ff" "question-9de0e52e-4e54-5cd5-8e58-4fda732ef76e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d0737b10-0304-5e2e-a18d-ef1cf02a07ff" :question/id #uuid "d0737b10-0304-5e2e-a18d-ef1cf02a07ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-332382" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-3},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{3}{s-1}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{3t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =2{e}^{3t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{3}{s-1}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}-3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\cdot t}-3{e}^{1\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}-3{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{3t}-3{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-df0f9134-af7b-577f-bb8b-2009b066b22f" "answer-field-43cb3dab-7c67-5df5-bb7f-1b8561a9585b" "answer-field-0abaee99-8d00-5498-8655-f03c7de5849a" "answer-field-67bc3df3-21d6-5ff8-936a-39854725ffb5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-df0f9134-af7b-577f-bb8b-2009b066b22f" :answer-field/id #uuid "df0f9134-af7b-577f-bb8b-2009b066b22f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-3c0a2880-de85-52e8-85de-0969492cdb58" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3c0a2880-de85-52e8-85de-0969492cdb58"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c0a2880-de85-52e8-85de-0969492cdb58" :answer/id #uuid "3c0a2880-de85-52e8-85de-0969492cdb58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-43cb3dab-7c67-5df5-bb7f-1b8561a9585b" :answer-field/id #uuid "43cb3dab-7c67-5df5-bb7f-1b8561a9585b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-357de87f-e9e1-5bed-9740-cf1a1c066776" :answer-field/choices ["answer-357de87f-e9e1-5bed-9740-cf1a1c066776"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-357de87f-e9e1-5bed-9740-cf1a1c066776" :answer/id #uuid "357de87f-e9e1-5bed-9740-cf1a1c066776" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0abaee99-8d00-5498-8655-f03c7de5849a" :answer-field/id #uuid "0abaee99-8d00-5498-8655-f03c7de5849a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a6acad7a-a7d5-50fe-94f8-03cc12e4ce79" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a6acad7a-a7d5-50fe-94f8-03cc12e4ce79"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6acad7a-a7d5-50fe-94f8-03cc12e4ce79" :answer/id #uuid "a6acad7a-a7d5-50fe-94f8-03cc12e4ce79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-67bc3df3-21d6-5ff8-936a-39854725ffb5" :answer-field/id #uuid "67bc3df3-21d6-5ff8-936a-39854725ffb5" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6ba96b2e-684a-5f93-b08a-1f0e2229610c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6ba96b2e-684a-5f93-b08a-1f0e2229610c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ba96b2e-684a-5f93-b08a-1f0e2229610c" :answer/id #uuid "6ba96b2e-684a-5f93-b08a-1f0e2229610c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9de0e52e-4e54-5cd5-8e58-4fda732ef76e" :question/id #uuid "9de0e52e-4e54-5cd5-8e58-4fda732ef76e" :question/math-academy-id "q-332388" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=-\\frac{2}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s-5}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{2t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{5t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{-\\frac{2}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =-2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2\\cdot t}+{e}^{5\\cdot t} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2t}+{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t} \\\\ -2{e}^{2t}+{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e8e0339e-584d-50e3-9d66-c4b5654e80f2" "answer-field-62b0c5b0-195a-52a8-a42e-0d7cdd505876" "answer-field-43acf565-70e8-59c8-9da0-7f2d6c9509f6" "answer-field-2dec9ee2-df88-5435-a628-2db834f23d11"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e8e0339e-584d-50e3-9d66-c4b5654e80f2" :answer-field/id #uuid "e8e0339e-584d-50e3-9d66-c4b5654e80f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-86aa83a1-0b94-57bd-b3df-ddec044a5317" :answer-field/choices ["answer-86aa83a1-0b94-57bd-b3df-ddec044a5317"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86aa83a1-0b94-57bd-b3df-ddec044a5317" :answer/id #uuid "86aa83a1-0b94-57bd-b3df-ddec044a5317" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-62b0c5b0-195a-52a8-a42e-0d7cdd505876" :answer-field/id #uuid "62b0c5b0-195a-52a8-a42e-0d7cdd505876" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9fa7dfaa-3002-551e-b29b-b70703cbc0de" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9fa7dfaa-3002-551e-b29b-b70703cbc0de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9fa7dfaa-3002-551e-b29b-b70703cbc0de" :answer/id #uuid "9fa7dfaa-3002-551e-b29b-b70703cbc0de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-43acf565-70e8-59c8-9da0-7f2d6c9509f6" :answer-field/id #uuid "43acf565-70e8-59c8-9da0-7f2d6c9509f6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-fdf95821-0667-5470-9d72-b2c2cd72e470" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fdf95821-0667-5470-9d72-b2c2cd72e470"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdf95821-0667-5470-9d72-b2c2cd72e470" :answer/id #uuid "fdf95821-0667-5470-9d72-b2c2cd72e470" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2dec9ee2-df88-5435-a628-2db834f23d11" :answer-field/id #uuid "2dec9ee2-df88-5435-a628-2db834f23d11" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ad88c67b-7dd2-5b78-a6b2-b39c461d1394" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ad88c67b-7dd2-5b78-a6b2-b39c461d1394"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad88c67b-7dd2-5b78-a6b2-b39c461d1394" :answer/id #uuid "ad88c67b-7dd2-5b78-a6b2-b39c461d1394" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-c6d426a1-c5fd-504b-b8a2-4f9281369271" :activity/id #uuid "c6d426a1-c5fd-504b-b8a2-4f9281369271" :activity/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049896 :activity/course 17592186046645 :activity/steps ["step-587c10b5-901c-515e-9d0a-14cb1187149f" "step-47bef454-c3f4-58da-9039-125730bb8c0a" "step-3f14c117-f925-5183-a5be-6eabe149b5f1" "step-d4a5ebcb-4913-519a-afda-77425f43427c" "step-0dcaece9-51e2-51f1-b644-f84c01d3c37c"] :activity/first-step "step-587c10b5-901c-515e-9d0a-14cb1187149f" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-587c10b5-901c-515e-9d0a-14cb1187149f" :step/id #uuid "587c10b5-901c-515e-9d0a-14cb1187149f" :step/content "question-d4b0fddb-f441-5332-9904-2f366a824fe8" :step/next "step-47bef454-c3f4-58da-9039-125730bb8c0a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-47bef454-c3f4-58da-9039-125730bb8c0a" :step/id #uuid "47bef454-c3f4-58da-9039-125730bb8c0a" :step/content "question-229cdf1d-b683-5de3-b351-27b1d6a26233" :step/next "step-3f14c117-f925-5183-a5be-6eabe149b5f1" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3f14c117-f925-5183-a5be-6eabe149b5f1" :step/id #uuid "3f14c117-f925-5183-a5be-6eabe149b5f1" :step/content "question-d0737b10-0304-5e2e-a18d-ef1cf02a07ff" :step/next "step-d4a5ebcb-4913-519a-afda-77425f43427c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d4a5ebcb-4913-519a-afda-77425f43427c" :step/id #uuid "d4a5ebcb-4913-519a-afda-77425f43427c" :step/content "question-9de0e52e-4e54-5cd5-8e58-4fda732ef76e" :step/next "step-0dcaece9-51e2-51f1-b644-f84c01d3c37c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0dcaece9-51e2-51f1-b644-f84c01d3c37c" :step/id #uuid "0dcaece9-51e2-51f1-b644-f84c01d3c37c" :step/content 17592186305036 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152153 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-50a1adba-14a0-5a88-abaf-07e0387210e6" "question-9d148965-74db-5cec-9065-74d36d2d9d5c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151941 :question/problem "Let $R = [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x+2y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152154 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-086ea7e4-b45d-5b48-92bf-b7fd8532a3af"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151942 :question/problem "Let $R = [0,1] \\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 10-x^2-y^2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152232 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-27a8dfe2-6a96-5884-8d1c-c8b7f914c19a" "question-c350d5bc-4404-57ee-b54b-285bbf9a8f0e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152042 :question/problem "Let $R = [2,3] \\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x - y + 3.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-50a1adba-14a0-5a88-abaf-07e0387210e6" :question/id #uuid "50a1adba-14a0-5a88-abaf-07e0387210e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-75306" :question/problem "Let $R=[3,4]\\times [-5,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=2x+y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x+y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x+y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/51/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e449d4e6-5069-5c0a-ac4d-1bc5e9e548d0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e449d4e6-5069-5c0a-ac4d-1bc5e9e548d0" :answer-field/id #uuid "e449d4e6-5069-5c0a-ac4d-1bc5e9e548d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-02b4f462-2c61-5567-8e86-726726c9ff96" :answer-field/choices ["answer-02b4f462-2c61-5567-8e86-726726c9ff96" "answer-f7c74500-e7ac-5eaa-beb4-4e1c203d88bc" "answer-bf3f732b-b276-53da-8c54-4876b853e7d0" "answer-02467f85-cb8c-52e6-8524-d58170a0e13a" "answer-a11f70f3-8e83-52f0-ae17-f28615c58f7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02b4f462-2c61-5567-8e86-726726c9ff96" :answer/id #uuid "02b4f462-2c61-5567-8e86-726726c9ff96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7c74500-e7ac-5eaa-beb4-4e1c203d88bc" :answer/id #uuid "f7c74500-e7ac-5eaa-beb4-4e1c203d88bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf3f732b-b276-53da-8c54-4876b853e7d0" :answer/id #uuid "bf3f732b-b276-53da-8c54-4876b853e7d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02467f85-cb8c-52e6-8524-d58170a0e13a" :answer/id #uuid "02467f85-cb8c-52e6-8524-d58170a0e13a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}_{i-1}+4{y}_{j-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a11f70f3-8e83-52f0-ae17-f28615c58f7b" :answer/id #uuid "a11f70f3-8e83-52f0-ae17-f28615c58f7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}_{i}+4{y}_{j}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9d148965-74db-5cec-9065-74d36d2d9d5c" :question/id #uuid "9d148965-74db-5cec-9065-74d36d2d9d5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-75307" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [1,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=5{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=5{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y$ increases as $x$ increases on $[0,2],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y)=5{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y$ increases as $y$ increases on $[1,5].$\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/51/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=5{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $5{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a4f8ba87-584e-5b9c-b10e-58f5d8d221b1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a4f8ba87-584e-5b9c-b10e-58f5d8d221b1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4f8ba87-584e-5b9c-b10e-58f5d8d