problem-5f50aa9a-2389-5024-b199-8e25913107a0" :assigned-problem/id #uuid "5f50aa9a-2389-5024-b199-8e25913107a0" :assigned-problem/content "multistep-f2d248c5-c3a9-5d9c-bcfc-f830bcac9594" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [17592186049940 17592186050789 17592186050277 17592186049835 17592186049327 17592186048946 17592186050902 17592186049507] :db/ensure [:assigned-problem/validate]} {:db/id "activity-7bfe2df4-f37e-5936-8ee1-635f7e4b77f4" :activity/id #uuid "7bfe2df4-f37e-5936-8ee1-635f7e4b77f4" :activity/title "Differentiating Polar Curves" :activity/type :activity.type/assignment :activity/steps ["step-6fa7716a-64b5-5197-92fc-82bb7b39f774"] :activity/first-step "step-6fa7716a-64b5-5197-92fc-82bb7b39f774" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-6fa7716a-64b5-5197-92fc-82bb7b39f774" :step/id #uuid "6fa7716a-64b5-5197-92fc-82bb7b39f774" :step/content "assigned-problem-5f50aa9a-2389-5024-b199-8e25913107a0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186062545 :answer-field/choices 17592186062546] [:db/retract 17592186062545 :answer-field/choices 17592186062547] [:db/retract 17592186062545 :answer-field/choices 17592186062548] [:db/retract 17592186062545 :answer-field/choices 17592186062550] {:db/id 17592186064577 :question/problem "Factor the following quadratic expression.\n\n$2{x}^{2}+7x+6=(x+\\,$\n{{field-1}}$)($\n{{field-2}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "We must factor the quadratic expression\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}+7x+6.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find two numbers that \n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant ($2\\times 6=12$), and\n\n- add to the linear coefficient ($7$).\n\nSince all coefficients are positive, we only need to consider the positive factor pairs of $12.$\n\nThe positive factor pairs of $12$ are\n\n$$\n(1,12),\\,(2,6),\\,(3,4).\n$$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(3,4)$ add to $7:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3+4 & =7\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we write the linear term as $3x+4x,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+7x+6 & = \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+3x+4x+6 & = \\\\ (2{x}^{2}+3x)+(4x+6) & = \\\\ x(2x+3)+2(2x+3) & = \\\\ (x+2)(2x+3) & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b6cbc592-2c25-5ac2-98cd-00aabe81a7d0" "answer-field-ed63e6cb-39c3-5d3f-a8c6-4ef7473abfa3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186061644 :answer-field/correct "answer-07a9d02b-b538-5620-b733-61af6ed20e19" :answer-field/choices ["answer-07a9d02b-b538-5620-b733-61af6ed20e19"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07a9d02b-b538-5620-b733-61af6ed20e19" :answer/id #uuid "07a9d02b-b538-5620-b733-61af6ed20e19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b6cbc592-2c25-5ac2-98cd-00aabe81a7d0" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6cbc592-2c25-5ac2-98cd-00aabe81a7d0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-dda4f1f8-6966-5ad9-a7a5-567211e5a9e0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dda4f1f8-6966-5ad9-a7a5-567211e5a9e0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dda4f1f8-6966-5ad9-a7a5-567211e5a9e0" :answer/id #uuid "dda4f1f8-6966-5ad9-a7a5-567211e5a9e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ed63e6cb-39c3-5d3f-a8c6-4ef7473abfa3" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed63e6cb-39c3-5d3f-a8c6-4ef7473abfa3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1a3001dc-c422-5f38-bf1a-6e6aac3baf6e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1a3001dc-c422-5f38-bf1a-6e6aac3baf6e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a3001dc-c422-5f38-bf1a-6e6aac3baf6e" :answer/id #uuid "1a3001dc-c422-5f38-bf1a-6e6aac3baf6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064279 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e0efe9ed-909f-5452-9389-702e59cbbd2e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e0efe9ed-909f-5452-9389-702e59cbbd2e" :question/id #uuid "e0efe9ed-909f-5452-9389-702e59cbbd2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-129415" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{64{p}^{2}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that $64$ and ${p}^{2}$ are both perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{64{p}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}\\cdot {p}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8\\cdot 8\\cdot p\\cdot p} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8\\cdot p\\cdot 8\\cdot p} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8p\\cdot 8p} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(8p)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity and simplify using the rules of absolute value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(8p)^{2}} & =|8p| \\\\  & =|8|\\cdot |p| \\\\  & =8|p|\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-30d23bc3-d1e0-5d77-9eab-3d40deacb024"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-30d23bc3-d1e0-5d77-9eab-3d40deacb024" :answer-field/id #uuid "30d23bc3-d1e0-5d77-9eab-3d40deacb024" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8dfd5123-ebf8-5f90-b7bf-84747508777c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-12ee5dfc-4b15-5556-8d87-0dc7c0550e16" "answer-b530d38a-61b2-52e5-8650-d0248f7c86d5" "answer-e2ead643-fa73-5935-bee6-e90b2db5ffe5" "answer-8dfd5123-ebf8-5f90-b7bf-84747508777c" "answer-119c39fb-efd6-5727-8c3b-adac3f25cf28"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12ee5dfc-4b15-5556-8d87-0dc7c0550e16" :answer/id #uuid "12ee5dfc-4b15-5556-8d87-0dc7c0550e16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16p" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b530d38a-61b2-52e5-8650-d0248f7c86d5" :answer/id #uuid "b530d38a-61b2-52e5-8650-d0248f7c86d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16|p|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2ead643-fa73-5935-bee6-e90b2db5ffe5" :answer/id #uuid "e2ead643-fa73-5935-bee6-e90b2db5ffe5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8p" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8dfd5123-ebf8-5f90-b7bf-84747508777c" :answer/id #uuid "8dfd5123-ebf8-5f90-b7bf-84747508777c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8|p|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-119c39fb-efd6-5727-8c3b-adac3f25cf28" :answer/id #uuid "119c39fb-efd6-5727-8c3b-adac3f25cf28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 8p" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064215 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3eaa9b96-57f5-5bea-bcf0-0afa03bea744"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3eaa9b96-57f5-5bea-bcf0-0afa03bea744" :question/id #uuid "3eaa9b96-57f5-5bea-bcf0-0afa03bea744" :question/math-academy-id "q-52181" :question/problem "$-{z}^{3}(4{z}^{2}-2z)=$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply each term inside the parentheses by the term outside the parentheses, simplify using the rules of exponents, and then we add the results together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{z}^{3}(4{z}^{2}-2z) & = \\\\ (-{z}^{3})(4{z}^{2})+(-{z}^{3})(-2z) & = \\\\ ((-1)\\cdot 4)({z}^{3}\\cdot {z}^{2})+((-1)\\cdot (-2))({z}^{3}\\cdot z) & = \\\\ (-4){z}^{3+2}+(2){z}^{3+1} & = \\\\ -4{z}^{5}+2{z}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a9aab190-eecc-5ce2-93c8-fa4f40aa1915"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a9aab190-eecc-5ce2-93c8-fa4f40aa1915" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9aab190-eecc-5ce2-93c8-fa4f40aa1915" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-728e061d-9d33-5b2a-a71d-aa061c66944c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-728e061d-9d33-5b2a-a71d-aa061c66944c" "answer-d208d9ba-b205-519b-92a8-913080237dda" "answer-3c38baae-067b-54f2-9239-4872cc86443c" "answer-8ea9c766-9b05-5b66-9fac-dab3d487277e" "answer-7e43acf4-e376-5667-81ea-3ec76bdc9f74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-728e061d-9d33-5b2a-a71d-aa061c66944c" :answer/id #uuid "728e061d-9d33-5b2a-a71d-aa061c66944c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4{z}^{5}+2{z}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d208d9ba-b205-519b-92a8-913080237dda" :answer/id #uuid "d208d9ba-b205-519b-92a8-913080237dda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4{z}^{5}-2z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c38baae-067b-54f2-9239-4872cc86443c" :answer/id #uuid "3c38baae-067b-54f2-9239-4872cc86443c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4{z}^{6}+2{z}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ea9c766-9b05-5b66-9fac-dab3d487277e" :answer/id #uuid "8ea9c766-9b05-5b66-9fac-dab3d487277e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4{z}^{6}+2{z}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e43acf4-e376-5667-81ea-3ec76bdc9f74" :answer/id #uuid "7e43acf4-e376-5667-81ea-3ec76bdc9f74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{z}^{2}+2{z}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105705 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-af48560b-05fb-5bc9-95de-b8bf00a67a5f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-af48560b-05fb-5bc9-95de-b8bf00a67a5f" :question/id #uuid "af48560b-05fb-5bc9-95de-b8bf00a67a5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-99627" :question/problem "$\\frac{63}{4\\sqrt{7}}=$" :question/worked-solution "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{7}$ from the denominator, all we need to do is multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{7}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{63}{4\\sqrt{7}} & = \\\\ \\frac{63}{4\\sqrt{7}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{7}} & = \\\\ \\frac{63\\sqrt{7}}{4\\cdot (\\sqrt{7})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{63\\sqrt{7}}{4\\cdot 7} & = \\\\ \\frac{9\\sqrt{7}}{4} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate 