57" :question/problem "Given that $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}}={x}^{n},$ what is $n?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the radical to a fractional exponent, and then we apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}} & = \\\\ {({x}^{3})}^{1/5} & = \\\\ {x}^{3\\cdot (1/5)} & = \\\\ {x}^{3/5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $n=\\frac{3}{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dd16cf0e-5f7d-51cc-ae14-ca512e5da309"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dd16cf0e-5f7d-51cc-ae14-ca512e5da309" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd16cf0e-5f7d-51cc-ae14-ca512e5da309" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3d2d9d98-d016-50d1-ade9-88cfcb3d34b5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ac3b342a-b178-519b-87a5-bbfeeed0b751" "answer-b116a718-63f8-5776-b375-ffe686801428" "answer-de25f1f1-df80-5532-ac59-dc389d2badfc" "answer-3d2d9d98-d016-50d1-ade9-88cfcb3d34b5" "answer-114b0dfa-89bf-5311-81ef-fcc7328f4d93"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac3b342a-b178-519b-87a5-bbfeeed0b751" :answer/id #uuid "ac3b342a-b178-519b-87a5-bbfeeed0b751" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b116a718-63f8-5776-b375-ffe686801428" :answer/id #uuid "b116a718-63f8-5776-b375-ffe686801428" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de25f1f1-df80-5532-ac59-dc389d2badfc" :answer/id #uuid "de25f1f1-df80-5532-ac59-dc389d2badfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d2d9d98-d016-50d1-ade9-88cfcb3d34b5" :answer/id #uuid "3d2d9d98-d016-50d1-ade9-88cfcb3d34b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-114b0dfa-89bf-5311-81ef-fcc7328f4d93" :answer/id #uuid "114b0dfa-89bf-5311-81ef-fcc7328f4d93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068785 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3861e4f2-43a8-5a8e-aa2e-58c7272cde17"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3861e4f2-43a8-5a8e-aa2e-58c7272cde17" :question/id #uuid "3861e4f2-43a8-5a8e-aa2e-58c7272cde17" :question/math-academy-id "q-73781" :question/problem "Which of the following values of $w$ satisfy the inequality $\\frac{w}{4}<5\\,?$\n\nI. $w=24$\n\nII. $w=20$\n\nIII. $w=8$" :question/worked-solution "We substitute each value into the given inequality and check to see if the resulting statement is true or false.\n\n- We substitute the value $w=24$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{w}{4} & <5 \\\\ \\frac{24}{4} & <5 \\\\ 6 & <5\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $w=24$ into the inequality leads to a **false** statement. \n\nTherefore, $w=24$ **does not satisfy** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $w=20$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{w}{4} & <5 \\\\ \\frac{20}{4} & <5 \\\\ 5 & <5\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $w=20$ into the inequality leads to a **false** statement. \n\nTherefore, $w=20$ **does not satisfy** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $w=8$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{w}{4} & <5 \\\\ \\frac{8}{4} & <5 \\\\ 2 & <5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $w=8$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $w=8$ **satisfies** this inequality." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-312e7e5a-ba75-54c4-a217-c2cd5f4576d2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-312e7e5a-ba75-54c4-a217-c2cd5f4576d2" :answer-field/id #uuid "312e7e5a-ba75-54c4-a217-c2cd5f4576d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-97d05aa0-8bf6-5cca-b33d-33d9