 :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-46fbea6e-db08-56e8-bb91-369d04b61064" :answer-field/choices ["answer-46fbea6e-db08-56e8-bb91-369d04b61064"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46fbea6e-db08-56e8-bb91-369d04b61064" :answer/id #uuid "46fbea6e-db08-56e8-bb91-369d04b61064" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068702 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6705c0b1-618f-5fe7-bac1-95db3808efcf" "question-850f2473-aeb8-5637-89c4-7aa5503f51fe" "question-6e8aaddd-953c-576c-ad6b-2e4d36b66988"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6705c0b1-618f-5fe7-bac1-95db3808efcf" :question/id #uuid "6705c0b1-618f-5fe7-bac1-95db3808efcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-74708" :question/problem "Evaluate $f(-2,1)$ if $f(x,y)=3x+y-1.$" :question/worked-solution "We substitute $x=-2$ and $y=1$ into the function definition and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =3x+y-1 \\\\ f(-2,1) & =3(-2)+(1)-1 \\\\  & =-6+1-1 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5564ea51-cc0b-5e12-842f-0baaf0e8fb4d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5564ea51-cc0b-5e12-842f-0baaf0e8fb4d" :answer-field/id #uuid "5564ea51-cc0b-5e12-842f-0baaf0e8fb4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-592a76e6-16ff-52d8-b0c4-12f0106d7cd3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5c487054-9369-5348-8f5d-ebbcbc9cf99b" "answer-592a76e6-16ff-52d8-b0c4-12f0106d7cd3" "answer-3ee72209-ec75-59db-9e99-4aaca2509c28" "answer-7f013d6b-cae1-5d91-a70a-41da8bc3bb79" "answer-56b921e3-4f54-54a8-990d-d79989274ac9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c487054-9369-5348-8f5d-ebbcbc9cf99b" :answer/id #uuid "5c487054-9369-5348-8f5d-ebbcbc9cf99b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-592a76e6-16ff-52d8-b0c4-12f0106d7cd3" :answer/id #uuid "592a76e6-16ff-52d8-b0c4-12f0106d7cd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ee72209-ec75-59db-9e99-4aaca2509c28" :answer/id #uuid "3ee72209-ec75-59db-9e99-4aaca2509c28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f013d6b-cae1-5d91-a70a-41da8bc3bb79" :answer/id #uuid "7f013d6b-cae1-5d91-a70a-41da8bc3bb79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56b921e3-4f54-54a8-990d-d79989274ac9" :answer/id #uuid "56b921e3-4f54-54a8-990d-d79989274ac9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179820 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ae08ca9c-939c-5021-b3a5-7c6bc6fdc648"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ae08ca9c-939c-5021-b3a5-7c6bc6fdc648" :question/id #uuid "ae08ca9c-939c-5021-b3a5-7c6bc6fdc648" :question/math-academy-id "q-93129" :question/problem "$40$ students took an algebra exam. If $12$ of them failed this exam, what percentage of students failed it?" :question/worked-solution "We're given a part and a whole, and we must find a percentage. So, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{percentage}=\\text{part}÷\\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn this case, \n\n- the part is the number of students that failed the exam, which is $12,$ and\n\n- the whole is the total number of students, which is $40.$\n\nSubstituting our numbers into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{percentage}=12÷40=\\frac{12}{40}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this fraction as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12}{40}=\\frac{12÷4}{40÷4}=\\frac{3}{10}\n$$\n\nTo write this as a percentage, we create an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{10}=\\frac{3\\times 10}{10\\times 10}=\\frac{30}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{30}{100}=30%\n$$\n\nTherefore, $30%$ of the students failed the exam." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b3071424-443b-5ed8-bef9-8dd32743f887"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b3071424-443b-5ed8-bef9-8dd32743f887" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3071424-443b-5ed8-bef9-8dd32743f887" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-37af64e4-e53f-5906-9205-2976cf8eff34" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b358ad10-6ca2-50e7-b950-ca22dadd8d53" "answer-f71d24b6-3be6-532f-aae7-679ccc049399" "answer-37af64e4-e53f-5906-9205-2976cf8eff34" "answer-51036995-cbd5-5e9c-b7fc-99756d59a10b" "answer-03a9e932-b2d8-57e4-8e26-371499db4a87"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b358ad10-6ca2-50e7-b950-ca22dadd8d53" :answer/id #uuid "b358ad10-6ca2-50e7-b950-ca22dadd8d53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f71d24b6-3be6-532f-aae7-679ccc049399" :answer/id #uuid "f71d24b6-3be6-532f-aae7-679ccc049399" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37af64e4-e53f-5906-9205-2976cf8eff34" :answer/id #uuid "37af64e4-e53f-5906-9205-2976cf8eff34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51036995-cbd5-5e9c-b7fc-99756d59a10b" :answer/id #uuid "51036995-cbd5-5e9c-b7fc-99756d59a10b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03a9e932-b2d8-57e4-8e26-371499db4a87" :answer/id #uuid "03a9e932-b2d8-57e4-8e26-371499db4a87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054835 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7841e502-bd87-5f16-9f68-b66396ece51e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7841e502-bd87-5f16-9f68-b66396ece51e" :question/id #uuid "7841e502-bd87-5f16-9f68-b66396ece51e" :question/math-academy-id "q-177595" :question/problem "If $-3=\\frac{a}{9},$ then $a=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\frac{a}{9}=-3\n$$\n\nIn this equation, $a$ is being divided by $9.$ To isolate $a$, we can perform the opposite operation, which is *multiplying* by $9.$ So, we multiply both sides of the equation by $9$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{9} & =-3 \\\\ 9\\cdot \\frac{a}{9} & =9\\cdot (-3) \\\\ \\frac{9a}{9} & =-27 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{9}a}{\\cancel{9}} & =-27 \\\\ a & =-27\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-883868e4-aa29-5d95-bf5d-f1c4c5b5efca"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-883868e4-aa29-5d95-bf5d-f1c4c5b5efca" :answer-field/id #uuid "883868e4-aa29-5d95-bf5d-f1c4c5b5efca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-077da333-cb04-5b90-b89f-4cc665733d05" :answer-field/choices ["answer-077da333-cb04-5b90-b89f-4cc665733d05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-077da333-cb04-5b90-b89f-4cc665733d05" :answer/id #uuid "077da333-cb04-5b90-b89f-4cc665733d05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064748 :question/problem "$\\frac{{z}^{18}}{{z}^{7}}=$" :question/worked-solution "We subtract the exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}^{18}}{{z}^{7}} & = \\\\ {z}^{(18-7)} & = \\\\ {z}^{11} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186062545 :answer-field/correct "answer-2780d2db-b5d8-51a7-86fb-49f658cee304" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2780d2db-b5d8-51a7-86fb-49f658cee304" "answer-8f5959f9-581b-5aad-9de2-fedc7cc48d68" "answer-730b8465-7159-5dad-8c03-b3cb57fc7371" "answer-e65f7a1f-1218-5ac9-9a4e-4255893b3a77"] :db/ensure [:answer-fiel